Limit: the census is not bit-for-bit and the header used to say it was. It compares ids plus each database file's presence, size and mtime; a writer that rewrote bytes in place at equal length and restored timestamps would pass. A read-only SQLite generation counter would close it and needs an open connection this half does not have.
Limit: planning is a time-of-check observation. It resolves paths and returns the strings it was given, so a component replaced by a symlink between planning and the first write is not caught here. The driver must re-verify identity immediately before its first mutation; that is the driver's obligation and the driver does not exist.
Limit: `productionIsReadable` checks that the database is a regular file and nothing more. Whether a later read is read-only is a property of how the driver opens it.
Ruled-out: treating every resolution failure as "the path does not exist yet" | measured: a self-referential symlink (ELOOP) was allowed as a realm path, because the failure took the missing-leaf branch and the lexical result looked clean.
Ruled-out: recording every stat failure as absence | measured: an unreadable parent turned a populated family into four absent rows, and two such censuses compared equal.
Ruled-out: checking only that realm paths sit outside production | the reverse containment is the dangerous one, because it is the direction that licenses deletion.
Ruled-out: resolving only the whole path and falling back to the lexical one | a `stateDir/escape` link to production with `escape/new.sqlite` as the database was allowed.
Ruled-out: a single mtime on state.sqlite as the census catch-all | under WAL a committed write leaves the main file byte-identical and grows the sidecar. Measured: two hundred inserts, main file unchanged, -wal past 800KB.
Ruled-out: comparing two multisets by joining and comparing strings | any element containing the delimiter splits across its neighbour. No delimiter choice fixes it, and the one first used here was a literal NUL.
Ruled-out: a RETRY disposition beside INCONCLUSIVE | every signal producing INCONCLUSIVE is a state where "did the side effect happen" is unanswerable, and the one thing that must not follow an unanswerable question is another message.
Ruled-out: matching a process by pid, or by name | pids are reused, and a name matches the peer Hermes instance that has to survive.
